  "overrides": {
    "notes": {
      "Vesuvi5/Inyo": "'Inyo' (1700 GU) demoted to a moon of 'Geki' (2200 GU) despite its name not saying 'Moon'. Accepted the generator's demotion: 'Inyo' is much smaller than 'Geki' and keeping it in 'Geki''s region preserves BC's original single-map grouping, per the brief's reasonable default.",
      "Vesuvi5/Mori": "'Mori' (1000 GU) demoted to a moon of 'Geki' (2200 GU) despite its name not saying 'Moon'. Accepted the generator's demotion: 'Mori' is much smaller than 'Geki' and keeping it in 'Geki''s region preserves BC's original single-map grouping, per the brief's reasonable default."
    },
    "star": {
      "star_class": "remnant_hot",
      "radius_gu": 2000.0,
      "why": "The star's core was destabilised by a Kessok Solarformer (BC's own opening: 'the star... its core is destabilising!'). What remains is a hot remnant: small, luminous, blue-white. BC's own lighting agrees -- Vesuvi 5's authored directional is (0.6, 0.6, 0.8). Radius stays 2000 GU so the system's geometry does not move."
    },
